From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:11:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/29] tests: hardening and pull-model test suite with a local
 GitHub API stub

rdgenerator/tests/ (replaces the empty tests.py), 45 tests, run with
`manage.py test rdgenerator`:

- ghstub.py: a threaded stand-in for api.github.com. It checks the bearer
  token, records every request, validates dispatch inputs like GitHub
  (declared names only, 65,535 characters), steps runs through
  queued/in_progress/completed, serves artifact zips through a 302 to a
  second "blob" port (and records whether Authorization reached it), and
  implements delete/cancel plus the bootstrap endpoints (repo create,
  secrets public key and sealed secret, Actions permissions, workflows).
  It is also runnable on its own for manual tests.
- test_security: settings refuse missing, published or short secrets, and
  env-file values stay out of os.environ. Login is required everywhere.
  Login, the generator and session API calls without a CSRF token get
  403. The API answers 401 without auth and accepts the bearer token
  without CSRF. The push-model endpoints are 404. /download and
  /api/download reject /proc/self/environ, ../, absolute paths,
  non-canonical uuids and names missing from the manifest. Validators
  accept upstream defaults and reject injections; filename sanitizing is
  tested.
- test_pull: the dispatch payload (inputs, ref, return_run_details, the
  decrypted zip members, images normalized to 256/512 px, no plaintext in
  the request), 413 for oversize images, 422 surfaced as 502, the
  unconfigured case. Poller: eager download, hostile zip members
  (traversal, symlink, junk) dropped, all artifacts and the run deleted,
  the token never sent to the blob host. Also: partial files kept on
  failure, the failed run deleted only after the keep window, success
  without artifacts, finding the run by name after a 204 dispatch,
  timeout cancel, size cap, 401 backoff without leaking the token,
  local prune.
- test_workflows: pullify --check is clean, only the expected workflows
  remain, every action is SHA-pinned. The server and runner validators
  agree. The setup job's decode script and decrypt.py are run as on a
  runner (heredoc GITHUB_ENV, masks, staged assets and patches, and
  rejection of a replayed cfg, a protocol mismatch, an injection and a
  flag/image mismatch).

